  "description": "I am 93 years with very poor mobility, as the result of which, I have recently acquired a Blue Badge and now receive Attendance Allowance. For the same lack of mobility reasons that I applied for the Blue Badge, I would like to have the roadside kerb in front of my house lowered and the wooden bollards placed in the grass verge in front of my home removed.  This is due to the fact that walking any distance is extremely painful for me and finding parking anywhere close to my home on Bilton Road, is usually impossible. I therefore need the kerb lowered so that any vehicles that collect me or drop me off, can park on my driveway, thereby minimising the distance that I need walk.  Additionally, it will allow my care providers to park on my driveway, when they attend my home to support me.",
